From 91ddd5d4b1c62ba070001ac08ef051181087f047 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tien Nguyen <tien.nguyen.uh@renesas.com>
Date: Fri, 8 Aug 2025 06:49:34 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] media: rzg2l-cru: fix retry path by stopping subdev with
 s_stream(0)

The retry thread was stopping the camera subdevice with
post_streamoff(), which does not actually stop the subdevice.
As a result, the next s_stream(1) failed and the camera would not
produce frames after a retry.

Observed WARN from the V4L2 core and the camera failed to stream after
a retry:
    WARNING: CPU: 0 PID: 539 at v4l2-subdev.c:442 call_s_stream+0xb8/0xe4
    pc : call_s_stream+0xb8/0xe4
    Call trace:
    call_s_stream+0xb8/0xe4
    retry_streaming_func+0x11c/0x1f0
    kthread+0x10c/0x110
    ret_from_fork+0x10/0x20
    irq event stamp: 132
    rzg2l-cru 10830000.video: CRU retry init: 1 times

Fix this by replacing post_streamoff() with:
    v4l2_subdev_call(sd, video, s_stream, 0);

This ensures the subdevice is cleanly stopped before restarting, which
restores streaming after retries and stabilizes the pipeline.

Upstream-Status: Pending

Signed-off-by: Tien Nguyen <tien.nguyen.uh@renesas.com>
---
 drivers/media/platform/renesas/rzg2l-cru/rzg2l-video.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/renesas/rzg2l-cru/rzg2l-video.c b/drivers/media/platform/renesas/rzg2l-cru/rzg2l-video.c
index 3e637d2b731a..54e38130a02c 100644
--- a/drivers/media/platform/renesas/rzg2l-cru/rzg2l-video.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/renesas/rzg2l-cru/rzg2l-video.c
@@ -671,7 +671,7 @@ static int retry_streaming_func(void *data)
 
 		/* Stop CRU reception */
 		rzg2l_cru_write(cru, ICnEN, 0);
-		v4l2_subdev_call(sd, video, post_streamoff);
+		v4l2_subdev_call(sd, video, s_stream, 0);
 		rzg2l_cru_stop_image_processing(cru);
 		pm_runtime_put(cru->dev);
 		msleep(20);
-- 
2.43.0

